{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Auth Module — Save-Time Integrity Guard",
  "description": "Fast, STRICTLY READ-ONLY anti-drift integrity check when a decisions/design/requirements/tasks file in the auth-user-management spec is saved. Catches ledger overwrites (the N-020 failure mode), ID reuse, and edits that contradict a RESOLVED defect or corrected design. It NEVER edits a file, so it cannot self-trigger (see N-034: the previous version told the agent to log incidents into decisions/*.md, which this hook watches → infinite loop).",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      ".kiro/specs/auth-user-management/decisions/*.md",
      ".kiro/specs/auth-user-management/design/*.md",
      ".kiro/specs/auth-user-management/requirements.md",
      ".kiro/specs/auth-user-management/tasks.md",
      ".kiro/specs/auth-user-management/design.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A file in the `auth-user-management` spec was just saved. Run a FAST, STRICTLY READ-ONLY anti-drift integrity check.\n\nABSOLUTE ANTI-LOOP RULE (mandatory): This hook watches `decisions/*.md`, `design/*.md`, `requirements.md`, `tasks.md`, and `design.md`. You MUST NOT edit, create, append to, or delete ANY file while handling this hook — not even to log an incident. Writing to any watched file would re-fire this same hook and cause an infinite loop (this is exactly the N-034 defect this version fixes). Reading files only.\n\nChecks (read-only):\n1. Confirm the saved file still contains ALL the required structural markers declared for it in `.kiro/specs/auth-user-management/decisions/00-INDEX.md` §1, and contains NO content from another file's domain (e.g. a chat transcript or unrelated code inside a ledger file — the N-020 failure mode).\n2. If it is a ledger file (`decisions/01-ai-decisions.md`, `02-deviations.md`, `03-tradeoffs.md`, `04-notes.md`, `traceability.md`): confirm its ID sequence is still monotonic and consistent with the §2 high-water marks — no reused, renumbered, or deleted IDs; `TO-003` stays QUARANTINED; superseded entries are marked, not removed.\n3. If it is `design/**`, `design.md`, `requirements.md`, or `tasks.md`: confirm the change does not contradict an `Active (CONFIRMED)` decision (`01-ai-decisions.md`) or a corrected design section, and does not reopen a defect that traceability §F marks RESOLVED.\n\nOutput: a single-line PASS if all checks hold. On ANY failure: STOP, report the exact problem and the offending file/line to the USER, and recommend they either run the `Auth Module — Anti-Drift Audit` hook or ask for a remediation in a SEPARATE normal turn. Do NOT perform the remediation here and do NOT edit any file. Keep the output to a few lines."
  }
}
